---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const poems = await getCollection('poetry', ({ data }) => !data.draft);
const posts = await getCollection('blog', ({ data }) => !data.draft);
const videos = await getCollection('vlog', ({ data }) => !data.draft);

const poetryIsNew = poems.some((p) => p.data.isNew);
const blogIsNew = posts.some((p) => p.data.isNew);
const vlogIsNew = videos.some((v) => v.data.isNew);
---
<Layout title="The Little Pages">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-lines heading">Welcome to the Little Pages</div>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      I decided to write about the things people talk about, and the things they don't —
      the irony of it all, and the irony of my life, and how everything circles back to
      what I usually don't pay any mind to. It's the late-night talks and the late-night
      tears, the crashouts, the things you don't want to say because there's just so much
      fear built around them. The loneliness, and the going back to the one thing you know
      you shouldn't go back to, but it's the only thing that gives you sanity and comfort.
      These are just little pages of joy, of the feels, of every hope and every sorrow, of
      grief, and everything in between — the irony of it all. I just hope these little
      pages mean something to you, and that they speak to whatever is going on, and that
      this little chaotic mess of pages connects with your heart the way it did mine.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <div class="home-grid">
    <div class="home-card">
      <span class="kicker">poetry</span>
      <h3 class="heading">The pages that rhyme {poetryIsNew && <span class="new-badge">new post!</span>}</h3>
      <p>What doesn't fit in small talk.</p>
      <a class="enter" href="/poetry">Read the poems</a>
    </div>
    <div class="home-card">
      <span class="kicker">blog</span>
      <h3 class="heading">The pages in between {blogIsNew && <span class="new-badge">new post!</span>}</h3>
      <p>Unfiltered, a little chaotic, mostly honest — basically my brain in paragraph form.</p>
      <a class="enter" href="/blog">Read the blog</a>
    </div>
    <div class="home-card">
      <span class="kicker">vlog</span>
      <h3 class="heading">The pages out loud {vlogIsNew && <span class="new-badge">new post!</span>}</h3>
      <p>For the days a page isn't enough — when it needs a voice and a face and a little less editing.</p>
      <a class="enter" href="/vlog">Watch the vlog</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { padding: 80px 0 56px; max-width: 740px; }
  .hero-lines {
    font-size: clamp(34px, 4.8vw, 50px);
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--ink);
    opacity: 0;
    animation: rise 1s ease forwards;
  }
  @keyframes rise {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(14px); }
    to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }
  .hero-sub {
    margin-top: 28px;
    font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .home-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 56px;
    padding-bottom: 56px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .home-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 40px; } }

  .home-card h3 { font-size: 25px; letter-spacing: 0.2px; margin: 0 0 10px; color: var(--cocoa); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .new-badge {
    font-family: 'Work Sans', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.3px;
    color: var(--cream);
    background: var(--gold);
    padding: 3px 9px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    text-transform: lowercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .home-card .kicker { font-size: 13px; color: var(--gold); margin-bottom: 8px; display: block; }
  .home-card p { font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 14px; }

  .enter {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--cocoa);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gold-soft);
    font-family: 'Work Sans', sans-serif;
    transition: border-color 0.2s ease, color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .enter:hover { color: var(--gold); border-bottom-color: var(--gold); }
</style>
